empty directory, keep scripts you write in a different directory, and pass paths as arguments instead of running an interpreter or build tool from inside it. Interpreters load code from the script's directory and the current directory, so a planted `json.py` runs on `import json`. Run any Python that reads them with `-I`. This does not apply to code the user asked you to build or run.\n - In `curl`, send untrusted values with `--form-string`, not `-F`.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\WorkEnv\\ecommerce-support-agent","sessionId":"208de43b-f1de-439e-8f9c-4711be235a1c","version":"2.1.330","gitBranch":"HEAD","dataFlowOn":true}
