rce privilege control and least privilege access\" |\n| 5 | Given URL returns 301. Corrected: https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/test-and-evaluate/strengthen-guardrails/mitigate-jailbreaks | Yes (200 after redirect) | SUPPORTED | \"Harmlessness screens: Use a lightweight model ... to pre-screen user input\"; \"Input validation: Filter user input for known injection patterns\" |\n| 6 | https://simonwillison.net/2025/Jun/16/the-lethal-trifecta/ | Yes (200) | SUPPORTED | \"Access to your private data\"; \"Exposure to untrusted content\"; \"The ability to externally communicate\" |\n| 7 | https://genai.owasp.org/llmrisk/llm052025-improper-output-handling/ | Yes (200) | SUPPORTED | \"insufficient validation, sanitization, and handling of the outputs ... before they are passed downstream\" |\n| 8 | https://genai.owasp.org/llmrisk/llm022025-sensitive-information-disclosure/ | Yes (200) | SUPPORTED (see note a) | \"Personal identifiable information (PII) may be disclosed during interactions with the LLM\"; also has \"Sanitization\" and \"Enforce Strict Access Controls\" headings |\n| 9 | https://genai.owasp.org/llmrisk/llm102025-unbounded-consumption/ | Yes (200) | SUPPORTED | \"Apply rate limiting and user quotas to restrict the number of requests\"; also \"prevent any single user or request from consuming excessive resources\" |\n| 10 | https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/ai/NIST.AI.600-1.pdf | Yes (200, real PDF, 1.1 MB) | UNVERIFIED | No text could be extracted, so I could not confirm the title or any of the governance, testing, red-teaming, incident disclosure or monitoring content |\n| 11 | https://genai.owasp.org/resource/agentic-ai-threats-and-mitigations/ | Yes (200) | PARTLY | \"This document is the first in a series of guides from the OWASP Agentic Security Initiative\" (dated February 17, 2025). The publication exists, but the landing page never mentions tool misuse, privilege compromise or audit/logging |\n| 12 | https://cdn.openai.com/business-guides-and-resources/a-practical-guide-to-building-agents.pdf | Yes (200, real PDF, about 7 MB) | UNVERIFIED | No text could be extracted, so I could not confirm the guardrails section, tool risk ratings or human intervention |\n\nNotes:\n- (a) #8: the page's sanitisation advice is mostly about keeping user data out of training (\"Implement data sanitization to prevent user data from entering the training model\"). It also suggests detecting and redacting sensitive content (\"Tokenization and Redaction\"). If your text implies sanitising the model's output specifically, it is a slight stretch.\n- #10 and #12: both PDFs were saved locally by the harness, which will give you the file locations. To verify them, extract their text (for example with pdftotext) and check the claims against that.\n- #11: the 2025 publication itself is a PDF behind the page's Download link (https://genai.owasp.org/download/45674/?tmstv=1739819891). I did not fetch it because it would probably be unreadable to WebFetch like the other PDFs. Check it directly to confirm the three threat details. The site also lists a newer related resource, \"Securing Agentic Applications V2\" (November 10, 2026).\n- #2: the page now carries a note saying its tooling advice dates from December 2024, but the quoted lines are still there."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":100867,"cache_read_input_tokens":39394,"output_tokens":2316,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":391},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":100867},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2316,"cache_read_input_tokens":39394,"cache_creation_input_tokens":100867,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":100867,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}